WEBVTT

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.360
I'd like to book a book for a friend of mine.

00:03:00.028 --> 00:03:00.668
this afternoon.

00:03:00.908 --> 00:03:01.568
A single room.

00:03:01.908 --> 00:03:02.408
A single room.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.480
For Mr. B. Johnson.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:05.744
He is dead.

00:03:06.268 --> 00:03:06.628
Fiance.

00:03:08.956 --> 00:03:10.176
That's right, man. Thank you very much.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.160
Any calls?

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:35.960
No, Mr. Carter.

00:03:44.172 --> 00:03:45.012
I don't know.

00:03:45.484 --> 00:03:47.004
How did he get on with the Wainwrights?

00:03:47.468 --> 00:03:48.448
Oh, fine.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.640
They're like every house.

00:03:51.084 --> 00:03:52.224
that wasn't for sale.

00:03:52.748 --> 00:03:54.268
What about the one in Pond Street?

00:03:54.408 --> 00:03:56.848
No, they're vaguely considering it.

00:03:57.324 --> 00:03:58.684
I'll send him some more particulars.

00:03:58.884 --> 00:03:59.844
You'd do that.

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:03.570
In about ten years, they might buy a chicken coop.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:04.950
There's a country for you.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.360
Everything takes time in the country.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.950
It's slow, but it's safe.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:13.170
Slow, Freddy.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:16.080
What you need is a nice cup of tea.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:19.660
Freddy, tell me something.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:23.860
How did the English resolve all their problems with a cup of tea?

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.900
Ah, the cup that cheers.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.980
You don't know it eight years.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:38.030
you never will eight years let's see that's 300 working days a year that's

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:44.220
2,400 times I've heard you say ah the cup that cheers at precisely four o'clock

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:51.130
in the afternoon fancy you noticing that I've also noticed we're getting to be

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:56.420
like the rest of Ashmore we're in a rut right so we are personally I get

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.420
enough excitement reading the Sunday newspapers

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:07.500
Yes, this is Mr. Curtis speaking.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.450
Oh, Mr. Linfors.

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:12.140
You like the house?

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:15.020
Oh, you don't like the house?

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:23.680
Yes.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.310
Okay, Mr. Linfors.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.130
Have a busy day.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.100
Let me take some of these.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:31.420
Thanks.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:36.540
Old man Lempfers wants the details on the milk place out in Dachem.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:41.210
Oh, I'm out right away.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.330
Oh, you're not going to be long, are you, darling?

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:44.570
My train goes at five.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:45.370
You up somewhere?

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.330
Oh, darling, you never listen.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.440
I'm going to stay with mother for a couple of days.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:50.380
I told you at breakfast.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.160
Oh, yes.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.190
What are those things?

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:54.850
Spending your money.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:56.340
I've been to the jumble sale.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:57.540
Anybody there?

00:05:58.280 --> 00:05:58.660
Everybody.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:05:59.970
Pity you couldn't get along.

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:05.940
Oh, hello.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:08.390
The Potters were there.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:09.750
She looks dottier than ever.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:10.980
Vicar in good form?

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:11.460
Oh, yes.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:12.860
Poor darling, but he's getting so thin.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:13.820
It's that wife of his.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:14.760
She nags him, I think.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:16.430
Anyway, she never stops talking.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:18.780
Oh, what are we doing Monday night, Freddy?

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:20.900
It's your turn to come to us, I think.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:21.560
Is it, darling?

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:27.240
Is it our turn to go to Freddy or Freddy's turn to come to us?

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.780
Um, our turn.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:34.840
Well, I guess there's nothing to keep me.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:37.490
Good. Help me with these things, will you?

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:38.790
You'll lock up, Freddy, huh?

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:39.650
Yes, Alan.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.710
And get that stuff out right away, will you, please?

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:49.150
Oh, Alan, every Thursday, Elizabeth comes here loaded weekend shopping.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.630
You say, well, I guess there's nothing to keep me here,

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:53.080
and you'll lock up, Freddy.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.200
That's been going on for eight years.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:56.640
I see your point.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.020
See you tomorrow.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:06:59.040
Yes, goodbye.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:08.490
What did Freddy say to you when you were leaving the office?

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.440
He thinks we're in a rush.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:12.070
Do you?

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:14.140
I talked a minute with him.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.980
I suppose everybody gets that way once in a while.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:19.220
I do.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:21.030
Then I go out and buy a new hat.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:28.680
As a natural fact, I wasn't going to bring it up until you were in a better mood.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:31.630
I got this today.

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:33.300
Do you like it?

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:36.080
You're going to put it in a cage?

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.980
Alan, what's the matter?

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:43.610
What's your work?

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:45.070
A nice house?

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:47.290
Yeah, scout meetings every Thursday.

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:49.490
We go to Freddy's every other Monday.

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:51.570
Every other Monday they come to us.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.680
We have dinner in town at least once a week.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:57.210
With your mother.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.830
You've gone back to the States after you left the Marines.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.010
You talk too much.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:17.990
Married some nice American girl.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.760
There's no need to make this an interracial problem.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:21.720
Can you manage?

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.710
Good afternoon, Miss Merchington.

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:26.720
Good afternoon, Mrs. Curtis.

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.550
Hello, Mr. Curtis.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:35.900
I'll only be gone for two or three days.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.240
Look after Mr. Curtis for me while I'm gone, will you?

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:39.400
I'd love to.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.840
I'll call in and say goodbye before I leave.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:44.760
She'd love to.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:47.630
Why saddle me with that withering aspen distress?

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:48.890
Darling, she'll hear you.

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:50.350
Well, you know she gives me the willies.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.120
Goodness, it's nearly four.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:56.130
She's a sweet person.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.980
I don't like going away feeling there's no one to look after you.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:08:59.480
Elizabeth.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:08:59.980
Oh, put...

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:05.890
You ought to make yourself take a holiday.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.450
What you need is a sniff of sea air.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.660
I wouldn't mind a weekend in Paris.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.300
Oh, darling, what would you do in Paris?

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:14.860
Give me that.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:17.380
You know what I like to do?

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:17.800
What?

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.510
We ought to go out sometime and get really plastered.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:21.970
Yes, dear.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:23.000
Oh, the time.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:42.240
Bye, darling.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:43.560
Take care of yourself.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:44.750
Listen.

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:46.490
Don't get on that train.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:46.690
What?

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:49.250
Come on, let's fly to Paris for sort of a second honeymoon.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:50.770
Darling, it's a lovely idea, but it's crazy.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:51.830
Well, let's be crazy. Come on.

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:53.360
The mother's waiting for me.

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:56.520
No, I wouldn't dream of disappointing mother.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:59.300
Helen isn't fair to upset me with the train.

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:01.020
Don't kill me!

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.940
Your husband has just been out. He said he'd be back in about an hour.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:53.770
I believe a young lady booked a room for me today.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.120
Your name, sir?

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:56.200
Johnson.

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:58.570
Oh, yes. Will you sign the register, please, sir?

00:10:58.970 --> 00:10:59.930
I've reserved your room.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:00.860
On the ground floor.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:03.620
Is it a bath?

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:05.880
No, sir, the bathroom is just next door.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:10.000
I stayed here some time ago.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:11.670
I had a room on the first floor.

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:12.590
Room six.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:14.300
Is it available by any chance?

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:15.340
I'm afraid not, sir.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.800
Room six is booked until next Monday.

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:17.540
Room two.

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:19.670
Si, thank you.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:31.220
Thank you.

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:35.690
Huh? Yes, sir? Any messages for me?

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:39.480
No, sir. I'm terribly sorry, sir. I thought you'd gone out.

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:42.740
Two gentlemen caught asking for you, sir, and they didn't leave their names.

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:50.540
Did they say if they were coming back?

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:52.020
No, sir.

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:21.350
Good evening, Mr. Curtis. Good evening, Tom. The usual? Double.

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:50.990
So you have a telephone here. Yes, at the end of the passage

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:07.870
Yes, sir.

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:14.030
I'm looking for a young lady who's class parked outside.

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:15.310
Star?

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:16.620
Pretty?

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:17.840
Yeah.

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:19.530
Yes, she is.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:21.800
Hello?

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:25.130
Has Mr. Johnson arrived at the hotel yet?

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:26.520
Yes, miss.

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:27.960
He arrived, but he's out at the moment.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.120
No, miss, I'm afraid he didn't.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.850
Oh, thank you.

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:50.760
Second, where is this telephone?

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.600
It's through that passageway, sir.

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:13.940
Barnum?

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:14.520
Yes, sir?

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:17.480
There's a door at the end of the passage you need to the car park also.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:21.280
Yes, come on.

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:28.840
Interesting.

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:29.500
Yes.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:30.430
Right.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:35.560
Well, good night time.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:36.420
Good night.

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:12.410
I'm sorry, but when I get stuck, I always haul up for one, too.

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:15.210
I tell you what, I live down the road about a half a mile.

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:16.630
I'll pull the garage from there.

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:18.530
Get in the car.

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:19.750
They'll pick it up from here.

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:50.620
wait in here i'll get on the phone sorry to be so much trouble that's okay didn't i see you with

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:57.660
the gold tonight did you yes you're in kind of a hurry your friends were disappointed they're not

00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:59.900
my friends those men have been pestering me

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:02.730
Oh, well, you should have gone to the police.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.210
I suppose I should have.

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:05.660
Hello?

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.420
Ashmore 230, please.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:08.410
I see.

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:09.740
Will you call me back?

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:10.800
Thank you.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:13.190
The line's busy.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:14.490
They're going to call me back.

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:16.030
I hope they won't be too long.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:17.270
I've got to get back to London tonight.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:18.770
You'd better take that coat off.

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:19.470
It's pretty wet.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:20.380
Thank you.

00:19:27.490 --> 00:19:27.850
Married?

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:28.500
Yes.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.540
I thought so.

00:19:31.260 --> 00:19:31.580
Why?

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:33.040
You look it.

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:36.200
Thanks for the compliment.

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:39.130
I was only making conversation.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:40.560
Would you like a drink?

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:41.920
Sounds wonderful.

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:48.050
You have a very good memory.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:55.460
Here's to married life.

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:01.420
She's, um, quite attractive.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:02.960
Yes, I'm lucky.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.830
It's quite a change that your husband say that.

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:06.600
Hmm?

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:09.790
Well, the ones I've met have been, um, misunderstood.

00:20:12.570 --> 00:20:13.430
Maybe it's a line.

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:14.870
Maybe.

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:24.120
Hello, Palmer's Garage.

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:26.720
Oh, Palmer, this is Alan Curtis.

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:29.980
A car belonging to a friend of mine has stalled about a half...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:35.070
half a mile past my place. Could you come over and take a look at her? Good. I'll meet you there.

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:43.000
Oh, I'm afraid I'm being a terrible nuisance. Do you want me to come with you?

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:47.550
Well, that's all right. I'll meet them there and see if we can get it started. I've got to get to London

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:53.720
tonight. Okay. Oh, uh, if the phone should... I won't answer.

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:07.640
I can't get a guy tonight, Mr. Curtis.

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:10.430
I'll let you have her at 10 in the morning.

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:11.550
That's the best I can do, sir.

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:12.980
Okay.

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:15.630
Well, get it ready as soon as you can, will you?

00:21:15.990 --> 00:21:16.630
Oh, I'll do that, sir.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.040
Excuse me.

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:23.320
It's all this car being towed in.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:24.560
I'm looking for the owner.

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:25.880
Oh, are you?

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.200
You brought it in, didn't you, sir?

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:29.610
Good night.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:30.820
You know, what's the testimony?

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:33.830
The owner of the car is in London.

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:36.250
I took it to the station 20 minutes ago.

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:37.780
That was all foolish of you.

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:39.740
Is that any of your business?

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.900
Yes, sir. We're police officers. CID.

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:42.780
Police?

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:44.500
Yes, could I have your name, please, sir?

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:46.380
Alan Curtis.

00:21:47.060 --> 00:21:47.660
Thank you, Mr. Curtis.

00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:51.420
I think you ought to know that the owner of the car is wanted for questioning.

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:55.160
What time did you say the train left?

00:21:58.190 --> 00:21:58.830
10.45.

00:21:59.050 --> 00:21:59.910
Mr. Curtis, sir.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.730
What's that?

00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:03.450
Well, the car's been picked up, aren't you?

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:06.780
Mr. Curtis, you won't be leaving Ashmore, will you?

00:22:07.850 --> 00:22:08.430
I doubt it.

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:10.190
We might want to see you again.

00:22:11.650 --> 00:22:11.930
Good night.

00:22:32.010 --> 00:22:39.170
Is that you?

00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:40.150
Yeah.

00:22:41.060 --> 00:22:41.920
I'm taking a bath.

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:42.740
Hope you don't mind.

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:44.210
Look, will you get out of there?

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:45.150
I want to talk to you.

00:22:45.730 --> 00:22:46.330
Sounds urgent.

00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:46.970
It is.

00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:58.440
It's out of action until morning.

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:02.740
I don't know how you're going to get back to London.

00:23:03.560 --> 00:23:05.520
Well, is there any place around you where I can hire a car?

00:23:05.700 --> 00:23:07.490
I doubt it.

00:23:09.290 --> 00:23:09.850
Anything wrong?

00:23:10.260 --> 00:23:10.480
Yes.

00:23:10.960 --> 00:23:14.460
Those men who've been pestering you all afternoon happen to be policemen.

00:23:15.350 --> 00:23:16.610
And don't tell me you didn't know.

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:18.500
Did you tell them where I was?

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:18.780
No.

00:23:19.100 --> 00:23:21.320
Now, look, I don't know who you are or what you've done,

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:23.980
but will you please get out of here in ten minutes?

00:23:24.180 --> 00:23:24.760
Don't be silly.

00:23:24.840 --> 00:23:26.120
No woman can change in ten minutes.

00:23:26.200 --> 00:23:26.940
Well, you can try.

00:23:27.610 --> 00:23:29.820
Oh, my bag's in the other room with my coat.

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:34.450
You'd better make yourself invisible.

00:23:40.420 --> 00:23:43.440
I just thought I'd pop in to see you have everything you want.

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:44.580
Oh, yes, I have. Thank you.

00:23:44.680 --> 00:23:45.520
What about supper?

00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:46.660
I've had supper out.

